A [[Gamorrean]] '''fighter''' was present in an [[Gor Koresh's Honky Tonk|arena]] in a [[Warehouse district (Carnita arena)|warehouse district]] fighting with [[Unidentified Gamorrean fighter 2|another Gamorrean]]<ref name="Chapter 9" /> in [[9 ABY]].<ref name="Date" /> [[Gor Koresh]] bet on the other Gamorrean to win in the next [[Standard minute|minute]]. Koresh then stood up and shot the Gamorrean.<ref name="Chapter 9" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|They're a little leaner. They're a little more of the fighting Gamorreans as opposed to the heftier Gamorrean guards from Jabba's palace.|Property master Josh Roth|<ref name="Making">{{DisneyGallery|Disney Gallery: The Mandalorian: Making of Season Two|Making of Season Two}}</ref>}}
The Gamorrean fighter first appeared in the official trailer for the [[The Mandalorian Season Two|second season]] of [[Jon Favreau]]'s [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', which was published on [[Wikipedia:YouTube|YouTube]] on [[September 15]], [[2020]].<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|eW7Twd85m2g|The Mandalorian &#124; Season 2 Official Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/the-mandalorian-season-2-official-trailer}}</ref> The fighter then appeared in ''The Mandalorian'' Season Two debut "[[Chapter 9: The Marshal]]," which was directed by Favreau<ref name="Chapter 9" /> and first aired on Disney+ on [[October 30]], 2020.<ref name="D23">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-october-2020|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in October 2020}}</ref> The Gamorrean was played by [[Barry Hanley]],<ref name="BH Instagram">{{Instagram|username=hammerinhanley73|url=p/CHL427iAlJB|name=[[Barry Hanley]]|quote=Clips from #mandalorian. Me on the left. Matt Shadden RIP on the right. Godspeed brother. #gamorrean #starwars #starwarsfan #gamorreanguard|archiveurl=https://archive.vn/xv0CW}}</ref> who was credited as a stunt performer<ref name="Chapter 9" /> but later confirmed his and<ref name="BH Instagram" /> fellow stunt performer [[Matthew Blake Shadden]]'s<ref name="Chapter 9" /> roles as the two fighters in the episode on [[Wikipedia:Instagram|Instagram]].<ref name="BH Instagram" />

The Gamorrean was made to be more leaner than the ones found in [[Boba Fett's Palace|Jabba's Palace]] in [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars:'' Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']]. The prop team led by property master [[Josh Roth]] made both the fighters' axes hollow [[Wikipedia:Aluminum|aluminum]] with an electric mechanism to present sparks every time the two axes clashed. For the Gamorrean fight, Favreau wanted it to be similar to a [[Wikipedia:Muay Thai|Muay Thai]] fight to lean the atmosphere of the episode into more of a gangster movie in contrast to other themes presented throughout ''The Mandalorian''. Stunt coordinator [[Ryan Watson]] helped direct the fighting, intending to present a strong and clumsy style in respect to other styles of fighting in the ''[[Star Wars]]'' universe.<ref name="Making" />

